================================================================================
KEY DIFFERENCES
================================================================================

Frontend vs Java Backend:
  - Frontend calls Backend REST; it never touches Canton or ML directly
  - Backend orchestrates: Risk Engine -> ML Service -> Canton -> MongoDB -> Chain

Java Backend vs Canton APIs:
  - Java Backend = business logic, fraud detection, consensus block builder
  - Canton API = immutable DAML ledger, cryptographic party signing
  - Backend uses CantonDamlJsonApiGateway to translate to Canton commands
  - Canton API returns Contract IDs; Backend returns business objects (txnId, status)
  - All Canton calls require JWT with actAs/readAs party claims

Canton API vs ML API:
  - Canton = append-only ledger, DAML templates, consensus-based, persistent
  - ML = stateless scoring, IsolationForest model, returns numeric anomaly scores
  - ML score feeds into Java Backend risk engine; Canton records the final outcome
  - Canton cryptographically signed; ML has no auth requirement

